This block unconditionally creates and appends a new `.mermaidTooltip` div every time `setupToolTips` is called (e.g., on chart re-render), leaking DOM nodes. `classDb.ts` correctly guards against this with `if (tooltipElem.empty())`. The equivalent guard is needed here:
```ts
if (select('.mermaidTooltip').empty()) {
  tooltipElem = select('body').append('div')…
}
```
